From 38a88e1730282425521209fc36fa8eb968dae611 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/24] ARM: dts: gts28ltexx: Bluetooth on UART3; M5 Wi-Fi with
 PERST# held high

- New exynos5433-gts28ltexx-bt.dtsi, included by the board file
  (section 13): BCM4358 Bluetooth on UART3 (hci_bcm, serdev), BT_EN
  gpd4-0, BT_WAKE gpr3-7, HOST_WAKE gpa2-2, PMIC 32 kHz clock. 460800
  baud: UART3 runs at 24 MHz here and 921600 gives UBRDIV = 0, after
  which the patched controller no longer answers.
- exynos5433-gts28ltexx-m5.dtsi keeps only Wi-Fi/PCIe (not in the
  default board until the firmware-start stall is solved). PERST#
  (gpr3-5) is held high as a GPIO output like the vendor driver does,
  CLKREQ# and gpr3-6 keep the PCIe function.
- Board header: section index completed (9-13).

Checked on the SM-T715: Bluetooth up from a cold boot with the
default DTB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
